From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: link the C++ runtime of the machine the native build runs on

The native build linked libstdc++ and libgcc statically, so the libraries
carried the builder's own copies. A builder whose distribution compiles
libstdc++.a for x86-64-v4 (CachyOS) then makes libraries that execute AVX-512
in std::locale's constructor the moment they are loaded: 1035 such
instructions, and SIGILL in QEMU on a host without AVX-512 (an Alder Lake
laptop) when the executor opened libdxvk_dxgi.so. Linked dynamically they use
the host's libstdc++.so, built for the host's CPU, as vkd3d-proton's native
build already does.
---
diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 4964301b..a8712997 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -167,11 +167,6 @@ else
   
   dxvk_name_prefix = 'dxvk_'
   dxvk_pkg_prefix = 'dxvk-'
-
-  link_args += [
-    '-static-libgcc',
-    '-static-libstdc++',
-  ]
 endif
 
 dxbc_spirv = subproject('dxbc-spirv')
